cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to Oxide, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Oxide"
abstract: >-
  Oxide is an open-source desktop terminal app that knows your GitHub
  Projects. It opens a Project and as many plain terminals as you like in its
  folder, with the Project's files, GitHub Issues and pull requests at hand.
authors:
  - family-names: Cavallini
    given-names: Lorenzo
  - name: "The Oxide contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/getoxide/oxide"
url: "https://github.com/getoxide/oxide"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - terminal
  - GitHub
  - pull requests
  - desktop app
  - Tauri
  - Rust
